e\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<-5) & =P(-\\infty <X<-5) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-5}4{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{e}^{4x}]}_{-\\infty }^{-5} \\\\  & ={e}^{-20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421866 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421864 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421866 1069 "q-87226" 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421866 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421866 1071 "Compute $P(X>3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421866 1072 #uuid "942a9198-9a9b-5910-a327-96717799bf91" 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421866 1074 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>3) & =P(3\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}]}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{81}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421867 1062 #uuid "01b175bd-e667-5a75-b3df-02b40ee2e81b" 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421867 1063 #edb/ref 17592186262578 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421868 1058 #edb/ref 17592186421867 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421868 1062 #uuid "1be2574c-a3ce-5ec0-bb9f-88e4dc8755a2" 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421868 1063 #edb/ref 17592186421866 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421869 1058 #edb/ref 17592186421868 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421869 1062 #uuid "fe10f7a6-87e1-5126-8846-1670d19ab5f3" 13194139534446 17592186045417 true] [17592186421869 1063 #edb/ref